WEBVTT

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:14.680
That's right. We...

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.140
No way...

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:48.640
What's going on?

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:51.310
Nia, Takatsuki...

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:53.960
Misao...

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.540
<i>Asura Cryin' 2</i>

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:28.520
"Future Without Memories"

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.270
We were swept up in Hagane's attack.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:40.710
And Naotaka...

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.560
...the first wold's Tomoharu...

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:45.440
...said he used Hagane's powers to come to the second world.

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.110
Then this world is...

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.690
It's not over yet.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:54.950
I should go to Rakurowa High School.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.890
The older Saeki will be there.

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:14.810
Excuse me...

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:15.750
Yes?

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.750
Oh, uh...

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:21.180
Do you know what happened to the First Student Council building?

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.450
First? What are you talking about?

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.180
We only have one student council.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:27.850
Oh, right.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.320
Could you be...

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:32.350
Huh?

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:33.230
I knew it!

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.110
The witch of Rakurowa High School's...

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.020
Witch?

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:38.340
Don't curse me!

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:38.160
Hey, wait!

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:41.750
What was that about?

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:44.740
A church...

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:46.800
I know!

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.710
"Nuns wanted. Pay starting at 15000 yen per day."

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:52.530
Shuri-san should be here.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:59.750
"Nun Cafe"

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:59.200
What is this?

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.340
Just one?

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.600
Oh, no. I...

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.390
Himezasa-san?

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:07.690
What?

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:11.240
One for non-smoking.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:14.410
Be penitent, lamb.

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:16.350
Oh, thank you.

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:20.960
Do you know Himezasa?

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.750
Oh, uh...

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:27.900
Yes, I suppose you could say that.

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:31.890
Himezasa is my older sister.

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:35.270
She died from an illness in middle school.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:36.710
She died?

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:40.380
She was born with a weak body.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:44.820
The doctors had told us she couldn't live long.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:48.990
But Rikka-chan never gave up on my sister.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:54.270
She worked hard to earn the money to provide her with the best medical care possible.

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:58.530
She's still stuck in the habit of working so hard...

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:01.120
...and opened this cafe.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.440
Is that so?

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.230
I'm glad to have had the chance to talk about my sister again.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.280
Please take your time.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:14.720
So Himezasa-san is gone...

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:17.740
You're that second year Tomoharu Natsume, right?

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:19.510
President Rikka...

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:20.920
...you know me?

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:23.500
Not president, but owner.

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:26.380
I graduated last year.

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:27.700
Graduated?

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:30.230
You graduate from high school after three years.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:33.840
Did you think I had been held back?

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.310
Oh, no. Of course not.

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:41.690
Well, even though I've graduated, I still hear a lot of rumors...

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:44.010
...like rumors about your girlfriend.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:45.360
Girlfriend?

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:47.410
You don't need to hide it.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:51.230
You're the boyfriend of the witch of Rakurowa High School, right?

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.320
Witches again?

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:52.760
Hey, listen...

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:54.170
...I heard your girlfriend...

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:54.170
Excuse me...

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:56.840
There's something I want to ask you.

00:05:57.310 --> 00:05:58.220
About what?

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:00.750
About the rumors about me and Rakurowa High School...

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.570
...among other things.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:03.690
Please.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:05.570
Is something going on?

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:07.650
Sure, I don't see why not.

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:09.890
Thank you.

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:14.380
It'll cost you extra.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:21.840
Even in this world, President Rikka is the same person.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.220
This world...

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:33.880
After graduating, President Rikka bought a church...

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:35.970
...and opened a nun cafe.

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:38.730
It's not Shuri-san's house here.

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:43.670
Reishiro is the president of Rakurowa High School's student council...

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.220
...and Shuri-san is the vice president.

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:50.190
This world is at least a year in the future.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:54.800
Have you ever heard the word "Asura Machina?"

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:56.440
"Asura Machina?"

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:59.120
Maybe you're familiar with burial dolls or daughters?

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:01.320
Is that some kind of slang?

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:04.820
Sorry, but we don't carry anything illegal.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.990
This really isn't the world I know.

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:11.540
I need to go back...

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.660
...but how?

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:16.950
Even if I made it back...

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:19.970
...I'd be facing people Shuri-san and Susugihara-san couldn't beat.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:23.820
Damn it...

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:30.900
What is that?

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.550
The color of the sky...

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:38.890
A daughter!

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:43.890
I thought these didn't exist over here.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:52.700
Watch out!

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:54.870
Come, Kurogane!

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.770
That's right. Kurogane was...

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:14.730
Stop!

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:26.190
Are you alright?

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:27.920
Stand back.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:29.150
You'll die.

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:48.630
It vanished...

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:51.010
Welcome to the first world...

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:52.860
...Tomoharu Natsume from the second.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.240
You know who I am?

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:58.090
I know more about you than you do.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:00.700
More?

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:03.790
Looks like we've got a lot of guests today.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:05.490
See you later, Tomoharu.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:10.190
Fighting with that beast...

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:12.660
I guess the rumors were true.

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:16.560
Do you know that girl?

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:18.500
You mean you don't?

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:21.670
She's the witch of Rakurowa High School.

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:26.870
"Kitsutaka"

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:31.690
How unnecessarily spacious...

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:38.890
Take a bath first. You smell terrible.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:40.030
Huh? Do I?

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.470
We'll talk after that.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.470
There's someone I want you to meet.

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:46.610
Someone you want me to meet?

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:48.410
Uh, who are you?

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:51.580
Right. I hadn't told you.

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:53.630
I'm Aki Kitsutaka.

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:57.750
So she's Aki-san...

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:01.600
President Toru's sister and President Kagayaki's...

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.110
Aki-chan, I didn't know you were in here.

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:14.430
Perfect timing.

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:17.960
Do you think you could help me take off these band-aids?

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:20.130
What's wrong?

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.570
Nothing!

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:22.630
I see.

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:23.800
Well, come on.

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:25.680
I can't reach them myself.

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:27.860
Come on, hurry up.

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:36.990
Hey! What do you think you're touching?

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:42.040
Aki-chan...

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:44.630
Thanks.

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:53.150
Forget everything you just saw!

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:55.060
I didn't see anything...

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:59.110
I guess it's my fault for not checking who you were.

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:01.460
Sorry for kicking you.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.930
I'm pretty sure you did a lot more than kick me.

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:06.460
Shut up!

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:07.780
Natsume-kun!

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:08.780
Takatsuki!

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:12.800
This is awful.

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:14.300
How did this happen?

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:15.390
Well, uh...

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:19.700
I'm glad you're okay, Takatsuki.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:21.820
What a relief.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:26.930
Are you the Natsume-kun I know?

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:28.750
Huh? Yeah...

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:32.390
We went to the beach together...

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:35.600
...and did that talent show at Saeki's house.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.800
The three-legged race for the sports festival.

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.000
I'm so happy to see you.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:46.930
What's up with you two?

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:49.720
Looks like she found who she was looking for.

00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:52.160
Oh, yes.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:53.720
Thank you.

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:55.450
What's going on?

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:56.980
Oh, um...

00:11:56.980 --> 00:12:01.030
I found her wandering the streets...

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:02.910
...three days ago.

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:05.910
Aki-chan can't help herself.

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:08.140
She brings home just about anything.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.430
So we're the same as stray cats?

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:14.520
Because of it, I got to see you.

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:16.020
You're right.

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:18.040
Thank you.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.420
Don't worry about it.

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:23.120
Is something burning?

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.930
Thanks for cooking dinner for me.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:36.550
Don't worry about it.

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:38.110
Kanade made it.

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:40.930
Yes. It did get a little burned, though...

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:44.130
Don't worry. It's still better than Toru's cooking.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:47.240
Look who's talking.

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:50.800
Delicious!

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:54.560
Your cooking is fantastic.

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:57.050
Stay as long as you like, Takatsuki-san.

00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.020
Oh, uh...

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:00.310
You can leave as soon as you like.

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:01.780
How cruel.

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:04.780
Tomoharu Natsume, right?

00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:06.280
Huh? Oh, yes.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:08.630
I knew your name sounded familiar.

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:11.800
Are you Naotaka Natsume's younger brother?

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:14.300
You know my brother?

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:17.640
We've never met, but I've heard of him.

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:18.610
Aki-chan...

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:21.320
What's going on?

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:22.810
"What's going on?"

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:24.280
Didn't he pass away?

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:25.930
He died?

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:27.250
It was a month ago.

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:31.040
I heard it was in the superstring gravity reactor accident.

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:32.710
Oh, right.

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:36.180
What happened in the accident?

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:39.120
Wouldn't you know more about that?

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:40.440
No, I...

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:48.140
The superstring gravity reactor Naotaka Natsume was working on got out of control...

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:50.310
...and he was caught up in the accident.

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:53.280
Superstring gravity reactor?

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:57.650
It was the world's top black hole generating facility.

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:01.320
President Kagayaki...

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:03.700
You...

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.550
It's your fault...

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:12.690
Natsume-kun.

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:14.010
Takatsuki...

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:16.510
This isn't him.

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.620
There must be a story behind that.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:23.590
Yes.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:26.150
Don't worry. I don't mind.

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:29.610
Did you finally decide to come out, freeloader?

00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:32.460
I heard we had some interesting guests.

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:35.050
Thanks for the food.

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:38.070
Let's see. What were we talking about?

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:41.390
Oh, right. The superstring gravity reactor.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:44.890
The superstring gravity reactor is...

00:14:44.890 --> 00:14:46.860
Don't talk with your mouth full.

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:49.090
Oh, sorry.

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:49.820
Oh, you.

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:51.500
Thanks.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:54.080
You're too easy on him.

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:59.050
The superstring gravity reactor isn't actually all that dangerous.

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:03.040
Small-scale black holes vanish immediately.

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:06.100
But that wasn't a small accident.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:07.270
About that...

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:10.390
Sorry.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:14.320
Under normal circumstances, there's no way such a large-scale accident would occur.

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:18.050
Something unexpected may have occurred.

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:25.070
You're our guest. You don't have to do that.

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:27.010
It's no trouble at all.

00:15:29.270 --> 00:15:32.920
Is Tokiya-san always like that?

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:34.710
Like what?

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:37.700
He seems kind of aloof...

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:39.940
...or maybe detached.

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:43.430
You can just call him slovenly.

00:15:43.930 --> 00:15:45.370
I think he is, too.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:50.010
Even though he acts like that, he's actually amazing.

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:54.740
He does a lot of research for foreign corporations.

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:56.590
Really?

00:15:56.940 --> 00:16:00.650
I just wish he'd try a little harder to be a decent person.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:03.170
My sister spoils him.

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:08.020
Do you mind if I ask you something a little weird?

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:13.370
If Tokiya-san chose to hurt another person...

00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:15.720
...what would you do?

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:19.970
I think I would help him achieve his goals.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.270
After all, I'm weak.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:23.470
Is that so?

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:25.500
But Aki-chan...

00:16:26.530 --> 00:16:28.490
If something like that happened...

00:16:28.990 --> 00:16:33.430
...I'm sure Aki-chan would be able to come up with an alternative.

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:37.860
I've been thinking about our world.

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:40.480
You know, like President Koala.

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:41.710
Oh, right.

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:46.940
We had a lot of fun.

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:47.680
Yes.

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:51.910
If Aki-san had been in our world...

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:57.280
...maybe President Kagayaki wouldn't have done those things.

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:00.720
It's possible.

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:06.180
But I'm glad I got to see you again.

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:08.410
I was worried about what might happen.

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:11.910
Yes. It's all thanks to Aki-san.

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:13.530
Yeah.

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:16.610
Now we need to find Misao and Nia.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:19.020
Misao-san isn't with you?

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:21.570
No matter how many times I call her, she doesn't appear.

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:24.540
She's usually around even when she isn't called.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:26.980
What could she be doing?

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:29.420
It will be okay.

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:30.210
Huh?

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:34.940
Misao-san would never leave you alone.

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:36.230
Takatsuki...

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:39.820
I'm sure you'll see her again soon.

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:41.640
Thanks.

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:44.600
I hope Nia's okay, too.

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:47.510
How are you, Takatsuki?

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:49.010
Are you vanishing?

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:50.570
Vanishing...

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:52.890
I'm fine.

00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:55.300
You can't possibly be fine.

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:58.760
I can't use my powers any more.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:00.760
Your demon powers?

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:03.050
The vanishing has stopped, too.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:06.810
Does that mean you've become a normal human in this world?

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:08.750
I don't know.

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:10.400
I see.

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:11.890
I'm sorry.

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:13.540
Huh? About what?

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:16.980
I won't be able to protect you.

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:21.350
Without my powers...

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:22.970
...I'm useless.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:24.380
Takatsuki...

00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:27.610
Misao-san and Nia-chan are gone.

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:29.340
Shuri-san, too.

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:33.190
I'm the only one here to protect you, but...

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:34.390
...but I...

00:18:35.390 --> 00:18:37.630
Takatsuki has always looked out for me.

00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:42.090
Despite her frail body, she's always been there.

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:43.910
Don't worry, Takatsuki.

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:47.850
As long as you're okay, it doesn't matter.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:50.230
But I can't protect you.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:52.640
You don't need to protect me any more.

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:56.630
It's my turn to do the defending.

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:58.920
I'll protect you, Takatsuki.

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:00.540
Natsume-kun...

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:03.360
Takatsuki, I...

00:19:13.900 --> 00:19:14.730
Again?

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:16.220
A stray daughter.

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:22.010
So it's a dragon this time?

00:19:23.420 --> 00:19:26.980
When did this world become full of demons?

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:32.590
Shufu, Kurenai, draw!

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:46.450
You've got a lot of nerve to attack the house of Kitsutaka.

00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:51.500
But as long as I'm here, I'll make sure no harm comes to our guests!

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:54.440
Natsume-kun...

00:19:55.060 --> 00:19:55.790
Aki-chan.

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:57.850
Let's leave this to Aki.

00:19:58.140 --> 00:19:58.730
But...

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:00.870
Aki will be fine.

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:03.550
Stay with me out of harm's way.

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:04.900
Tokiya...

00:20:13.300 --> 00:20:14.770
She sure is strong.

00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:17.120
Why is she so strong?

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:19.700
I can't imagine how much training that must take.

00:20:21.230 --> 00:20:23.610
According to Aki...

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:28.550
...no matter how hard a person trains, she will never be faster than a beast.

00:20:29.340 --> 00:20:32.450
Despite that, humans are still able to hunt animals...

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:33.920
...with willpower.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:36.450
Willpower?

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:37.680
The desire to win.

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:39.410
The will to protect.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.320
Intention makes humans stronger.

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:45.230
That must be why Aki is so strong.

00:21:02.470 --> 00:21:03.770
Good work, Aki.

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:05.770
Thanks. Is everyone okay?

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:07.260
Yes, thanks to you.

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:13.520
Aki-chan!

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:14.370
Behind you!

00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:26.000
The Kitsutaka sisters took you in?

00:21:26.740 --> 00:21:28.270
I guess you had enough luck.

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:31.440
The witch of Rakurowa High School.

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:34.080
That nickname isn't accurate.

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:38.750
I'm not a witch.

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:39.810
I'm a demon.

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:42.160
The luck eater's power...

00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:45.240
Are you Nia?

00:21:47.150 --> 00:21:49.800
I've waited five years, Tomoharu, Kanade.

00:23:20.860 --> 00:23:24.210
Your kindness is the problem.

00:23:24.650 --> 00:23:28.380
I can't ignore how real this feels.

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:30.870
Blue, red, black, white.

00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:32.070
Clear.

00:23:32.570 --> 00:23:34.980
"Adjoined Death and Peace"
